module estradiolExtractionQC
module estradiolMSDetection

manifest BloodSample
manifest DCM_Acetone_8020
manifest Methanol
manifest Isooctane
manifest EstradiolStandard
manifest EstrogenFreeSerum

// ============================================================
// Droplet-Scale Estrogen Assays in Breast Tissue, Blood, and Serum
// Mousa, Jebrail, Yang, Abdelgawad, Metalnikov, Chen,
// Wheeler, Casper -- Sci. Transl. Med. 1, 1ra2 (2009).
// DOI: 10.1126/scitranslmed.3000105
//
// Wheeler Lab (University of Toronto) / Casper Lab (Mount Sinai)
//
// PROTOCOL SUMMARY (Method 1 -- used in most experiments):
//   A 1-uL aliquot of whole blood, serum, or breast tissue
//   homogenate is loaded into a DMF device.  The sample is
//   allowed to dry on the electrode surface.  A series of
//   DCM/acetone (80:20 v/v) lysing-solvent droplets is then
//   driven over the dried sample to lyse cells and dissolve
//   steroids.  Methanol (polar extraction solvent) is dispensed
//   over the dried lysate to dissolve the steroids into solution.
//   The dissolved droplet is driven into an isooctane (non-polar
//   extracting solvent) reservoir and circulated for ~20 s to
//   partition away interfering compounds.  The polar phase is
//   driven to the collection reservoir.  This lysis-extraction
//   cycle is repeated (9 x 1.1-uL or 5 x 2.2-uL reservoir
//   volumes of methanol) until the sample reservoir is exhausted.
//   All collected droplets are pooled, dried, and reconstituted
//   for downstream analysis (ELISA or LC-MS/MS).
//
// PLATFORM:  Digital microfluidics (EWOD) with individually
//   addressable ITO electrodes (1.5-mm pitch) on a glass
//   substrate coated with Teflon-AF (dielectric).  Open-top
//   (single-plate) configuration.  A photoresist "wall" defines
//   the liquid-liquid extraction zone separating the isooctane
//   pool from the collection reservoir.
//
// SAMPLE VOLUME:  1 uL (1000-4000x smaller than conventional
//   biopsy methods).  Processing time ~10-20 min by DMF vs
//   5-6 h by conventional pipetting/centrifugation.
//
// DETECTION:
//   (i)  ELISA (ALPCO Diagnostics estradiol kit, abs 450 nm) --
//        used for recovery (86-119%, CV 7-10%) and precision.
//   (ii) LC-MS/MS with SRM (m/z 271/145) using a QTRAP system;
//        estradiol retention time ~3.2 min (isocratic MeOH/H2O
//        80:20, 2.1-mm x 50-mm Thermo Gold C18 column).
//   (iii) Direct MS (LTQ, negative mode, 250 C, 0.5 uL/min):
//        estradiol fragment m/z 183 confirmed absent in whole
//        samples but dominant in DMF-extracted samples.
//
// RECOVERY:  DMF-based recoveries 86-119% (ELISA). Breast
//   tissue: 522 pg estradiol / mg tissue (CV 1%, replicate 1-uL
//   samples from postmenopausal breast cancer patient).
//
// NOTE ON LYSIS ABSTRACTION:
//   Paper M&M: "a series of reservoir volumes (9 x 1.1 uL or
//   5 x 2.2 uL) of DCM/acetone was dispensed and driven dropwise
//   to the sample, each allowed to incubate until dry (~1 min)."
//   BioScript has no loop primitive, so each lysis sub-droplet
//   is modelled as a separate dispense + mix step.  A 3-cycle
//   representative encoding is used (covering the first lysis
//   wave); all cycles are chemically identical.  `mix` here
//   abstracts the electrode-driven translation, merging, and
//   incubation-to-dryness event, not a conventional mixing step.
//
// NOTE ON METHANOL EXTRACTION ABSTRACTION:
//   Paper M&M: "step three was repeated with successive reservoir
//   volumes of methanol (total 9 x 1.1 uL or 5 x 2.2 uL)."
//   Three methanol extraction cycles are encoded; each cycle
//   produces one extract droplet that is circulated in isooctane
//   (~20 s) before being driven to the collection reservoir.
//   The `heat` at 25c for 20s in each extraction cycle models
//   the ~20 s circulation event in the isooctane pool (room temp).
//
// NOTE ON FLUID OWNERSHIP:
//   Each dispensed fluid variable is consumed exactly once.
//   `heat` is void/in-place; the variable remains valid and is
//   subsequently consumed by `mix` or `dispose`/`drain`.
//   After the if-else QC gate, `drain` is used in the else
//   branch; `dispose` is used in the if branch (established
//   compiler pattern for QC gates per dataset conventions).
//
// NOTE ON h DURATION TOKEN:
//   The BioScript compiler (lilott8/BioScript) does not support
//   the `h` duration token.  All durations use `s` or `m`.
//   Reconstitution and analysis steps encoded in minutes.
//
// NOTE ON NON-ASCII CHARACTERS:
//   All comments and identifiers use ASCII only to avoid ANTLR4
//   UnicodeDecodeError at compile time.
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main            -- entry: lysis, methanol extraction,
//                           liquid-liquid partitioning in
//                           isooctane, pooling of extracts
//   BB2  extractPass     -- extractionSignal > 0: valid estradiol
//                           signal detected by ELISA proxy;
//                           dispose pooled extract
//   BB3  extractFail     -- extractionSignal <= 0: no signal
//                           (extraction failed); drain
//   BB4  extractJoin     -- join: MS confirmation branch begins
//   BB5  msPass          -- msSignal > 0: estradiol fragment
//                           m/z 183 / 271-145 confirmed; dispose
//   BB6  msFail          -- msSignal <= 0: analyte not confirmed;
//                           drain
//   BB7  finalCleanup    -- terminal: dispose QC signal droplets
// ============================================================

instructions:

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 1: Load sample.
//   An aliquot of whole blood (1 uL) is positioned in the
//   sample reservoir of the DMF device.  Blood and tissue
//   samples are allowed to dry on the electrode surface before
//   the top plate is affixed and solvents are loaded.
//   Standard estradiol solutions are used immediately without
//   pre-drying.  Here the blood sample is dispensed and modelled
//   as the starting material variable throughout the protocol.
//   Drying time: ~1 min per reservoir volume at room temperature.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

bloodSample     = dispense 1 units of BloodSample

// Drying at room temperature (25 C) for 60 s models the
// ~1 min incubation-to-dryness step for the sample droplet
// before lysis solvent is applied.  `heat` is void/in-place;
// bloodSample remains valid and is consumed at STEP 2.
heat bloodSample at 25c for 60s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 2: Lysis -- DCM/acetone wave, cycle 1 of 3.
//   DCM/acetone (80:20 v/v) dispensed from reservoir and
//   driven dropwise over the dried sample.  Incubation until
//   dry lyses cells and dissolves lipids / protein matrix
//   to free the steroid analytes.  `mix` abstracts electrode-
//   driven translation and merge + incubation-to-dryness.
//   Paper: 9 x 1.1 uL or 5 x 2.2 uL DCM/acetone per sample.
//   Three cycles encoded here as representative.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

lysisSolvent1   = dispense 1 units of DCM_Acetone_8020
lysate1         = mix bloodSample with lysisSolvent1 for 60s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 3: Lysis -- DCM/acetone wave, cycle 2 of 3.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

lysisSolvent2   = dispense 1 units of DCM_Acetone_8020
lysate2         = mix lysate1 with lysisSolvent2 for 60s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 4: Lysis -- DCM/acetone wave, cycle 3 of 3.
//   After three cycles the dried lysate contains the
//   free steroids (estradiol) ready for methanol dissolution.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

lysisSolvent3   = dispense 1 units of DCM_Acetone_8020
driedLysate     = mix lysate2 with lysisSolvent3 for 60s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 5: Methanol extraction -- dissolution cycle 1 of 3.
//   A reservoir volume of methanol (polar extraction solvent)
//   is dispensed and driven by DMF to the dried lysate to
//   dissolve the steroids into the polar phase.
//   Paper M&M: "a reservoir volume of methanol (1.1 or 2.2 uL)
//   was dispensed and driven by DMF to the dried lysate to
//   dissolve the steroids."
// ------------------------------------------------------------

methanol1       = dispense 1 units of Methanol
dissolvedSample1 = mix driedLysate with methanol1 for 10s

// Liquid-liquid extraction in isooctane (cycle 1):
//   A unit droplet of the dissolved sample (200-400 nL) is
//   driven to the isooctane reservoir and circulated within
//   the pool for ~20 s (modelled as heat at 25c for 20s)
//   before being driven to the collection reservoir.
//   Isooctane partitions away lipid-soluble interferents
//   (e.g. porphyrin m/z 715, DNA helicase m/z 677).
isooctane1      = dispense 1 units of Isooctane
extractDrop1    = mix dissolvedSample1 with isooctane1 for 10s
heat extractDrop1 at 25c for 20s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 6: Methanol extraction -- dissolution cycle 2 of 3.
//   Paper M&M: "step three was repeated with successive reservoir
//   volumes of methanol to extract all free estradiol."
// ------------------------------------------------------------

methanol2       = dispense 1 units of Methanol
dissolvedSample2 = mix extractDrop1 with methanol2 for 10s

isooctane2      = dispense 1 units of Isooctane
extractDrop2    = mix dissolvedSample2 with isooctane2 for 10s
heat extractDrop2 at 25c for 20s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 7: Methanol extraction -- dissolution cycle 3 of 3.
//   Final methanol pass exhausts the sample reservoir.
//   All extract droplets (cycles 1-3) are pooled in the
//   collection reservoir and allowed to dry at -20 C for storage.
//   `mix` here pools the running extract with the final cycle.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

methanol3       = dispense 1 units of Methanol
dissolvedSample3 = mix extractDrop2 with methanol3 for 10s

isooctane3      = dispense 1 units of Isooctane
extractDrop3    = mix dissolvedSample3 with isooctane3 for 10s
heat extractDrop3 at 25c for 20s

// Pool all extract droplets into the collection reservoir.
// Paper: "all extract droplets were pooled in the output
// reservoir and allowed to dry."  The final collected pool
// is modelled as the merge of the three extract cycles.
estrogenFreeSerumDiluent = dispense 1 units of EstrogenFreeSerum
pooledExtract   = mix extractDrop3 with estrogenFreeSerumDiluent for 5s

// Reconstitution: pooled extract is dried then reconstituted
// in 30 uL methanol/DCM (2:1 v/v) before analysis.
// Modelled as a room-temperature incubation (drying step).
heat pooledExtract at 25c for 5m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 8: ELISA extraction QC.
//   Paper M&M: "estradiol-specific ELISA (ALPCO Diagnostics)
//   used to evaluate recovery and precision of the DMF method."
//   estradiolExtractionQC module abstracts the plate reader
//   readout (abs 450 nm, mQuant spectrophotometer).
//   Final concentrations evaluated: 40, 1200, 3000, 6000 pg/mL.
//   Recovery 86-119%; CV 7-10% (Fig. 4, paper).
//   Breast tissue (independent patient): 522 pg/mg, CV 1%.
//   QC gate: if ELISA signal > 0, extraction is valid.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

extractionSignal = detect estradiolExtractionQC on pooledExtract for 30s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: Extraction QC gate
// Pass (BB2): extractionSignal > 0 -> estradiol signal detected;
//             dispose pooled extract and proceed to MS branch.
// Fail (BB3): extractionSignal <= 0 -> no signal (extraction
//             failure, reagent issue); drain and stop.
// Both branches converge at BB4 (extractJoin).
// ============================================================

if (extractionSignal > 0) {
    dispose pooledExtract
} else {
    drain pooledExtract
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: extractJoin
// Dispose ELISA QC signal. Control falls into MS confirmation
// branch (BB5/BB6).
// ============================================================

dispose extractionSignal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 9: MS confirmation.
//   Paper: LTQ mass spectrometer (negative mode, 250 C,
//   0.5 uL/min nanoelectrospray).  Estradiol fragment m/z 183
//   detected as highest-magnitude peak in DMF-extracted samples
//   but absent in non-extracted whole blood/serum (Fig. 2).
//   LC-MS/MS SRM (m/z 271/145) at retention time ~3.2 min
//   used for quantification from standard solutions, breast
//   tissue homogenate, and whole blood (Fig. 3, paper).
//   estradiolMSDetection module abstracts both the direct MS
//   and LC-MS/MS SRM readout steps.
//   A fresh standard solution is dispensed as the MS reference
//   analyte alongside the reconstituted extract.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

estradiolStd    = dispense 1 units of EstradiolStandard
msSignal        = detect estradiolMSDetection on estradiolStd for 192s

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: MS confirmation gate
// Pass (BB5): msSignal > 0 -> estradiol fragment m/z 183 /
//             SRM 271-145 confirmed at ~3.2 min retention;
//             dispose standard and signal.
// Fail (BB6): msSignal <= 0 -> analyte not confirmed (ion
//             suppression or extraction failure); drain.
// Both branches converge at BB7 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (msSignal > 0) {
    dispose estradiolStd
} else {
    drain estradiolStd
}

// ============================================================
// BB7: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose MS QC signal droplet. Experiment ends.
// ============================================================

dispose msSignal

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]
